# Ship only what the image needs.
#
# This is an allow-list: everything is excluded first, so anything that happens
# to sit in the working directory when the image is built -- deployment config,
# TLS material, scratch scripts, the source geodatabases under data/ -- cannot
# end up in an image layer by accident.
*

# Application
!app.py
!router.py
!requirements.txt
!assets

# Pre-built network. load_graph() prefers graph.p and falls back to graph.gml,
# which is the one present on a clean checkout, i.e. in CI.
!graph.p
!graph.gml

# Keep the directory update_output() writes into, but not the cached routes:
# docker-compose shadows it with a volume, a plain docker run does not.
!gpx
gpx/*

# Run by the CI workflow as: docker run velorouter python3 test.py
!test.py

!LICENSE
